Subject: [PATCH] Verify V4 recovery receipts and typed failure evidence

Preserve the default V3 and typed host-guard recovery cases while explicitly enabling V4 candidate storage for the existing real complete-block forks. Check durable journal-clear plus terminal receipts, exact historical parent-root failure facts, wrong acknowledgement fences, idempotent acknowledgement after reopen and bounded causal descendant exclusion.

Exercise completed, clock-deferred and operational source-restoration outcomes without invalidity facts; inconclusive execution retains its pending checkpoint. Retain the exact journal creation/per-call cap regression in both modes. Require pending-propagation and causally excluded targets to refuse new preparation without changing state.

Use explicit local corruption fixtures with valid storage wrappers and recomputed journal checksums to reject wrong mode/version, malformed evidence and incorrect parent/profile/historical-root tuples without advancing recovery or reconstructing a permanent fact. Existing immutable consensus body vectors are unchanged; local checksums are not an adversarial database authentication claim.

Strict Debug passes against frozen storage 13e4a138e (root 3ed3c26ed) and coordinator 3e79d498a. Independent Release passes 2/2 with the identical test-source digest. Commit only the assigned test source and new v4-test-evidence.md; borrowed production dependencies, CMake and the preexisting README are excluded.
